          "date": "2026-11-24 14:18:37.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18687 build: remove unused configure checks",
        "message": "LU-18687 build: remove unused configure checks\n\nSeveral configure checks defined macros that no code tested, so\nevery configure run compiled test programs for nothing.\n\nRemove the checks for HAVE_CACHE_DETAIL_WRITERS,\nHAVE_LINUX_BIO_INTEGRITY_HEADER, HAVE_EXT4_INFO_DQUOT,\nHAVE_FSCRYPT_SET_CONTEXT, HAVE_NLA_GET_S32 and HAVE_NLA_GET_S64.\n\nRemove the unused HAVE_LOCKS_LOCK_FILE_WAIT, HAVE_LM_GRANT_2ARGS,\nHAVE_GENERIC_FILEATTR_HAS_MASK_ARG, HAVE_MEMDESC_FLAGS_T and\nHAVE_OPENSSL_GETSEPOL from checks that also define a macro that is\nstill used.\n\nRemove the --disable-fail-alloc configure option.  It only defined\nRANDOM_FAIL_ALLOC, which nothing tested, so the option had no\neffect.  Also remove its fail-alloc Debian build profile.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7d6b09dcae4a902975a8331899a36faf6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
